00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:07,400
Rhombus

2
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:21,420
Observing rhombus ABCD in picture beside we have:

3
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:32,770
Side AB parallel side DC.

4
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:43,650
Side AD parallel side BC.

5
00:00:43,650 --> 00:01:00,800
4 sides AB, BC, CD, DA have equal lengths.

6
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:11,570
Conclusion: In rhombus then two pairs of opposite sides parallel to each other.

7
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:18,500
Length of 4 sides all equal.

8
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:29,600
Observing rhombus in picture beside we have:

9
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:42,050
Two diagonals AC and BD perpendicular to each other.

10
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:52,520
Length of two segments OA and OC equal each other.

11
00:01:52,700 --> 00:02:04,670
Length of two segments OB and OD equal each other.

12
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:13,520
Thus, every rhombus has characteristics below:

13
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:22,000
Two pairs of opposite sides parallel to each other.

14
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,570
Length of 4 sides all equal.

15
00:02:29,570 --> 00:02:39,870
Two diagonals perpendicular to each other at midpoint of each diagonal.

